# R47 Track D1 — the BOOL cell of the primitive-receiver E_NoMethodFound class.
#
# A sibling of `sh_reject_to_string_on_float.gg` on the RECEIVER-KIND axis. The
# float cell alone could pass for a numeric-only story (a numeric payload landing
# in a `Str` slot); this one can only pass if the admission decision is the
# receiver's method TABLE rather than the method's NAME. Rust gg:
# `error[E_NoMethodFound]: no method `to_string` found on type `bool``.
#
# RED-verified on the pre-fix self-host driver: it ACCEPTED this program and
# CC-failed with `incompatible types when assigning to type 'Str' from type
# 'int'` — the identical mint as the float cell, which is what establishes the
# two as one class rather than two anecdotes.
#
# CORRECT behaviour: `gg check` REJECTS this program on every lane.
void main():
    bool b = true
    print(b.to_string())
